WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.880
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:11.680
Today, you are going to see how one area&nbsp;
of research can unlock new capabilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:19.280
on a seemingly completely different area. We&nbsp;
are now living the advent of amazing AI-based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:26.560
language models. For instance, OpenAI’s GPT-3&nbsp;
technique is capable of all kinds of wizardry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:33.360
for instance, finishing our sentences, or creating&nbsp;
plots, spreadsheets, mathematical formulae,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:41.760
and many other things. While their Dall-E 2 AI is&nbsp;
capable of generating incredible quality images&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:48.720
from our written descriptions. Even if&nbsp;
they are too specific. Way too specific.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:55.600
Now note that all this wizardry is possible as&nbsp;
long as we are dealing with text and images.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.800
But how about, endowing a real&nbsp;
robot, moving around in the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.680
world with this kind of understanding of&nbsp;
language. I wonder what that could do?

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:14.080
Well, check this out! Scenario 1. This little&nbsp;
robot it uses GPT-3 and other language models,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:20.240
and it not only understands it, but it&nbsp;
can also use this knowledge to help us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.160
Don’t believe it? Have a look. For instance,&nbsp;
we can tell it that we spilled the coke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:32.400
and ask it how it can help us out? And,&nbsp;
it recommends finding the coke can,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:38.160
picking it up, going to the trash can,&nbsp;
throwing it out, and bringing us a sponge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:46.160
Yes, we will have to do the rest of it ourselves,&nbsp;
but still, wow, good job, little robot.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:52.720
Now the key here is that it not only understands&nbsp;
what we are asking, propose how to help, but,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:59.680
hold on to your papers, because here comes&nbsp;
Scenario 2. Oh my! It also looks around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:06.960
locates the most important objects required,&nbsp;
and now, it knows enough to make recommendations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:14.880
as to what to do. And of course, not all of&nbsp;
these make sense. Look at that! It can say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.880
it is very sorry about the mess. Well, thank&nbsp;
you for the emotional support, little robot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:27.840
but we also need a little physical help&nbsp;
here. Oh yes, that’s better. And now, look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:37.360
it uses its eyes to look around, yes, I have my&nbsp;
hand, well, does it work? Yes it does, great, now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:48.080
coke can, trash can, sponge. Hmm…it’s&nbsp;
time to make a cunning plan. Perfect!

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.920
And, it can also do plenty more. For instance,&nbsp;
if we’ve been reading research papers all day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.720
and we feel a little tired, if we tell&nbsp;
it, it can bring us a water bottle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:10.320
hand it to us, and can even bring us an apple.&nbsp;
Now I’d love to see this…be gentle, and! Oh&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:17.760
my! Thank you so much! The amenities at Google&nbsp;
HQ seem to have leveled up to the next level.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.880
And, believe it or not, these were&nbsp;
just really simple things, it can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:29.920
way better. Look. This is a plan that&nbsp;
requires planning 16 steps ahead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:36.720
and it does not get stuck, and doesn’t mess&nbsp;
up too badly anywhere. This one is as close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:43.840
to a personal butler as it gets. Absolutely&nbsp;
incredible. These are finally real robots that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:50.320
can help us with real tasks in the real&nbsp;
world. So cool! What a time to be alive!

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:57.760
Now, this is a truly amazing paper, but&nbsp;
make no mistake, not even this is perfect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:05.520
For instance, the success rate for the planning is&nbsp;
about 70%, and it can properly execute the plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.960
most of the time, but clearly, not all&nbsp;
the time. The longer term planning results&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:16.080
may also need to be a bit cherry-picked to&nbsp;
get a good one. It doesn’t always succeed.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:23.840
Also, note that all this is played at&nbsp;
10x speed, so, it takes a while. Clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:29.040
typing the message and waiting for the robot&nbsp;
still takes longer than just doing the work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:36.080
However, this is an excellent opportunity&nbsp;
for us to apply the First Law Of Papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:42.320
which says, that research is a process. Do not&nbsp;
look at where we are, look at where we will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:50.720
two more papers down the line. If OpenAI’s image&nbsp;
generator AI, DALL-E looked like this, and just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:58.240
a year and a paper later, it looks like this.&nbsp;
Well, just imagine what this will be able to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.280
just a couple more papers down the line.&nbsp;
And, what do you think? Does this get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.320
your mind going? If you have ideas for cool&nbsp;
applications, let me know in the comments below!

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.000
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

